<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tell Khaiber</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tell Khaiber is an archaeological site in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, about 20 kilometres north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, excavated from 2013 by the Ur Region Archaeology Project. Its principal building, a large fortified administrative complex, yielded an archive of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> tablets from the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sealand-dynasty">Sealand Dynasty</a> in the mid-2nd millennium BCE. The texts record the collection of grain and dates and the organisation of labour, giving a rare view of the Sealand state.</p></div>
